# AgenticSystemCore vocabulary — alignments to neighbouring vocabularies (INFORMATIVE).
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
# To the extent possible under law, the authors have waived all copyright and related
# or neighbouring rights to this file (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).
#
# What this file is. A small set of SKOS mapping statements from terms of
# ontology/agsc.ttl to terms of other vocabularies, so that a reader who knows one of
# them can find its nearest counterpart here. It is NOT part of the vocabulary: no rule
# of spec/ emits it, no build writes it to any route (AGSC-06-01's route set is closed),
# and ontology/agsc.ttl does not import it. AGSC-05-28 forbids the vocabulary to ship a
# property no rule emits, which is why these statements live beside it and not in it
# (an informative alignment, published beside the ontology and not in it). It adds no term:
# every subject below is one of the 52 terms of ontology/agsc.ttl, which
# tests/ontology/alignments.test.js checks.
#
# Why SKOS mapping properties and no owl:equivalentClass. Equivalence would assert that
# every instance of one class is an instance of the other; nothing read for this file
# supports that for any pair, so the weaker, documented SKOS relations are used:
# closeMatch ("sufficiently similar that they can be used interchangeably in some
# information retrieval applications"), narrowMatch/broadMatch (the target is narrower
# or broader) and relatedMatch (associated). A reasoner that loads this file together
# with SKOS will type both ends of each statement as skos:Concept (the mapping
# properties are sub-properties of skos:semanticRelation, whose domain and range are
# skos:Concept); that entailment is the second reason this file is kept out of the
# OWL 2 RL vocabulary (AGSC-05-22, AGSC-05-26a).
#
# Every target namespace and term was read at its source on 2026-09-23:
#
#   agento: <http://www.w3id.org/agentic-ai/onto#> — AgentO, the Agentic AI Ontology
#     (Kurniawan et al., TU Wien; ontology licence CC BY 4.0 as the file states).
#     Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/agentic-patterns/agentic-ai-onto/main/ontology.ttl
#     Quotes: "@prefix : <http://www.w3id.org/agentic-ai/onto#> ." and
#     "<http://www.w3id.org/agentic-ai/onto> rdf:type owl:Ontology" with
#     owl:versionInfo "1.1". Class comments quoted from that file:
#       KnowledgeBase   "A structured collection of information that an agent can reference."
#       Memory          "A knowledge structure that stores and retrieves past information,
#                        experiences, or states to support learning and decision-making."
#       WorkflowPattern "A reusable and structured template that defines a sequence or logic
#                        of tasks and interactions within an agentic workflow."
#       Constraint      "A rule or condition derived from the knowledge base that restricts or
#                        guides agent behavior or decision-making."
#       hasSubPattern   "Indicates a sub-pattern that is part of a larger workflow pattern."
#     Note: the namespace is written with "http://www." exactly as the file declares it;
#     this file does not depend on that host resolving.
#
#   dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> — W3C Data Catalog Vocabulary (DCAT) Version 3.
#     Source: https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-3/
#     Quote (Class: Dataset): "Definition: A collection of data, published or curated by
#     a single agent, and available for access or download in one or more representations."
#
#   skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> — SKOS Reference (W3C Recommendation).
#     Source: https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/
#     Quote: "skos:closeMatch is used to link two concepts that are sufficiently similar
#     that they can be used interchangeably in some information retrieval applications."
#
# The agent-memory vocabularies publish no term an alignment could point at yet: the
# W3C AI Agent Memory Interoperability Community Group has adopted a charter and
# published no report, and COGX is a file format with no RDF vocabulary. PROV-O is
# already aligned by rdfs:subClassOf inside ontology/agsc.ttl (Episode, Proposal and Review under prov:Activity; Gate, Procedure and Harness under
# prov:Plan; Source and Attachment under prov:Entity), so it is not restated here.

@prefix agento: <http://www.w3id.org/agentic-ai/onto#> .
@prefix asc: <https://w3id.org/agentic-system-core/ns#> .
@prefix dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

# A Bundle is a published, curated collection of knowledge an agent can reference.
asc:Bundle
    skos:closeMatch agento:KnowledgeBase, dcat:Dataset ;
    skos:relatedMatch agento:Memory .

# A Concept of kind "pattern" is a workflow pattern; Concept itself is broader.
asc:Concept
    skos:narrowMatch agento:WorkflowPattern .

# A Gate is a declared set of checks a change must pass.
asc:Gate
    skos:relatedMatch agento:Constraint .

# A Lesson is knowledge distilled from past Episodes.
asc:Lesson
    skos:relatedMatch agento:Memory .

# A Procedure is a reusable plan: trigger, steps and checks.
asc:Procedure
    skos:closeMatch agento:WorkflowPattern .

# asc:uses — the subject draws on the object; AgentO composes patterns with hasSubPattern.
asc:uses
    skos:relatedMatch agento:hasSubPattern .
